  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2019) position, SOLO basis, primarily from the bank's own audited Balance Sheet, Profit and Loss Account and the 'Highlights on the overall activities of the bank' annexure in that year's own annual report. Internal inconsistency found and resolved: the Capital Adequacy Pillar III narrative text states a minimum-capital-requirement (with buffer) of Tk.7,184.17m and a surplus of Tk.1,186.90m, but this does not reconcile with the independently, doubly-confirmed RWA of Tk.56,834,432,585 (appearing identically in this report's own Basel note and in the FY2020 report's comparative column) at the stated 12.50% rate (56,834.43 x 0.125 = 7,104.30m, not 7,184.17m). This report's own Annexure ('Highlights') table and its own Directors'-Report 5-year table both independently agree on a capital surplus of Tk.1,266,759,532 (implying MCR=7,104.30m), which is the figure this dataset uses; the Pillar III narrative's 7,184.17m/1,186.90m appears to be an isolated typo in that one paragraph. EPS: this report's own P&L states 1.55 for FY2019 and RESTATES FY2018 (its own comparative column) to 1.41, while the Directors' 5-year table in this SAME report shows FY2018 as 1.55 (unrestated) -- i.e. the bonus-adjustment is applied in the audited P&L comparative but not in the narrative 5-year table, within the same annual report. See sources.json for the bank-wide note. Total Capital, CRAR, CET1%/Tier2% and RWA are all directly reported; Tier-I/Tier-II absolute amounts were not legibly extracted from the Pillar III sub-table (values merged/blank) and are left as a gap rather than approximated a second way in the same year.",
